      "id": "claim_1d9dcd83582d4619bfc09ad19b9c76e5",
      "statement": "Gadget code is compiled on demand through the LOADER worker-loader binding, cache-keyed overseerId + codeVersion (+ chatId.sequence when chat-scoped) + gadgetId; a gadget pinned in the chat loads from the chat's content as of the snapshotted sequence while an unpinned committed gadget loads from its head commit, and every merge bumps codeVersion so head movement invalidates cached loads.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/overseer.ts#L3958-L4028",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4790257a5afd07d0881686d372e2392b85d28ff3e1d1708ee63a0a2c030e1c58:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_34afd1b842f54dd5a63faa4ee8d0064f",
      "statement": "The gadget worker definition uses mainModule server.js with all gadget .js files as modules, the allow_irrevocable_stub_storage flag for persistent stubs, and globalOutbound null — the gadget worker has no internet access; its env is built by getEnvForLoader as a plain object containing GADGET (a loopback to its own DO) plus one loopback per visible binding edge, each carrying caller {from:'gadget', chatId, gadgetId} for attribution.",
