      "id": "claim_f5892a6cdf784be3819acd4c9d806df9",
      "statement": "Gadget hooks use persistent stubs: a gadget implements [restore](params) and calls ctx.restore(params) to mint a persistent callback stub; within executeCode the agent forges such stubs on a gadget's behalf via the restore-forger capability (env.GADGET[restore](params)), which resolves the binding name against the execution's own binding map and lives only as long as the run() call.",
